---
// Privacy.
//
// THE ONE TRUST PAGE THAT CAN BE WRITTEN IN FULL TODAY, because it describes
// what the code does rather than a fact only Ric holds. Every sentence below is
// checkable against this repo, and that is the standard it is written to — a
// privacy policy assembled from a template is the same lie as an invented
// delivery cost, just longer and less likely to be read.
//
// CLAUDE.md requires this page and a working marketing opt-out with the first
// deploy. The honest form of the opt-out here is that there is no marketing list
// and nothing subscribes anyone to one: the only use of an email address is the
// receipt the buyer asked for. That is a statement to keep true rather than a
// box to tick — if a mailing list is ever added, this page changes first.
//
// Deliberately NOT dated. A "last updated" line is a fact like any other and it
// is the first thing to rot; the file's history in the repo is the real record.
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { GATEWAY_NAME } from "../../functions/api/_daraja.js";
import { known, site } from "../lib/site";

/* The networks the footer actually links to, so the sentence below names only
   those and disappears with them. Validated in lib/site.ts before this runs. */
const networks = [known(site.social?.facebook) && "Facebook", known(site.social?.instagram) && "Instagram"].filter(
  (name): name is string => typeof name === "string"
);
---

<Base
  title="Privacy — MomentAura"
  description="What this site collects, what it does not, and how long anything is kept."
  system="light"
>
  <section class="page">
    <div class="wrap page__inner">
      <h1 class="page__heading">Privacy</h1>

      <p class="page__body">
        This page describes what the site actually does. Everything here can be checked
        against how the site behaves.
      </p>

      <hr class="page__hair" />

      <h2 class="page__sub">What is not collected</h2>
      <!-- Cloudflare Web Analytics is switched on for the Pages project, so
           Cloudflare injects its beacon into every page at the edge. It is not
           in the repo and not in dist/, which makes it invisible to V4 and to
           every other gate: the build stays green whether this paragraph is true
           or not. This paragraph is the only place the site's own copy admits
           the beacon exists. If Web Analytics is ever switched off in the Pages
           dashboard, revert this paragraph in the same change. Every claim about
           what it records is taken from developers.cloudflare.com/web-analytics
           (data-origin-and-collection, faq); none of those pages mention
           cookies, so this paragraph does not either. -->
      <p class="page__body">
        The site counts page visits with Cloudflare's own analytics. Every page loads one
        script for it from Cloudflare's servers, at static.cloudflareinsights.com, which
        reports each page view and how long the page took to load. Cloudflare's
        documentation says it does not record the part of an address after a question
        mark, does not follow a visitor from one website to another, and keeps every
        report for 7 days and about one in ten after that. There are no tracking pixels,
        no advertising tags and no session recording. The fonts are served from this site
        rather than from a font network, so loading a page does not tell anyone else that
        you did.
      </p>
      <p class="page__body">
        There are no accounts and no passwords, so there is no store of credentials to
        lose. There are no cookies. Checking an order needs its reference and the phone
        number it was placed with, and nothing more.
      </p>
      <!-- functions/api/_throttle.js: a miss is counted in KV under the
           connecting address for one ten-minute window, and the key expires
           after twenty minutes. A successful lookup writes nothing. -->
      <p class="page__body">
        If an order lookup finds nothing, the internet address it came from is counted
        for ten minutes, so that guessing at other people's orders cannot go on without
        limit. The count is deleted automatically after twenty minutes. A lookup that
        finds your order is not recorded.
      </p>

      <h2 class="page__sub">What your browser stores</h2>
      <p class="page__body">
        Your order is kept in your own browser's local storage while you shop, and it
        holds only the product code and how many of each — never a name, a price or a
        stock figure. It never leaves your device until you go to checkout. Clearing your
        browser data removes it, and nothing here can read it back.
      </p>
      <p class="page__body">
        When you place an order, the browser also keeps the order reference,
        the {GATEWAY_NAME} payment request ID, the time the order was placed, and the product codes and
        quantities of that order, so the confirmation page can still show what you bought.
        It stays until your next order replaces it or you clear your browser data.
      </p>

      <h2 class="page__sub">What is collected when you order</h2>
      <p class="page__body">
        Your name, your phone number, where the order is going — the county, the area or
        estate, and a landmark — and an email address if you choose to give one. The
        email is optional and is not used for anything except a receipt. Nothing
        subscribes you to anything, because there is no mailing list to subscribe to.
      </p>
      <!-- functions/api/_daraja.js stkPush(): the request carries the phone number
           (PartyA, PhoneNumber), the amount, the order reference
           (AccountReference) and "MomentAura <reference>" (TransactionDesc).
           The name, the email and the delivery details are not in it. -->
      <p class="page__body">
        Your phone number is required because {GATEWAY_NAME} sends the payment prompt to
        it. To take the payment, {GATEWAY_NAME} is given your phone number, the amount and
        the order reference. Your name, your email and your delivery details are not sent
        to {GATEWAY_NAME}.
      </p>
      <p class="page__body">
        <strong>No card details are ever entered on this site.</strong> The payment
        prompt arrives on your own phone and you enter your PIN there, so your PIN never
        passes through this site. This site has no card form anywhere in it and never
        will.
      </p>

      <h2 class="page__sub">How long it is kept</h2>
      <p class="page__body">
        An order — the product codes, the quantities, the amount, your name, your phone
        number, the delivery county, area and landmark, the email if you gave one, and
        once it is paid the {GATEWAY_NAME} receipt number — is held for seven days from
        the last time it changed: when it is placed, and again when the payment is
        confirmed or fails. That is so the payment can be matched to the order and so you
        can look it up. After that it expires automatically.
      </p>

      <h2 class="page__sub">Who else sees it</h2>
      <p class="page__body">
        The person who runs MomentAura. {GATEWAY_NAME}, which sees the payment details
        listed above because it is taking the payment. The company hosting this site, because the pages and the order have
        to pass through it. Your delivery details are used to get the order to you.
        Nothing is sold, shared for advertising, or handed to a data broker.
      </p>

      <h2 class="page__sub">WhatsApp, social pages and email</h2>
      <p class="page__body">
        Tapping a WhatsApp link on this site opens WhatsApp. That conversation is handled
        by WhatsApp, which is owned by Meta, under WhatsApp's own privacy policy rather
        than this one. This site sends nothing to WhatsApp until you tap a link. The
        message it starts with carries a short code naming the page you tapped it on, such
        as WEB-CONTACT, and you can see and change it before you send.
        {
          networks.length > 0 && (
            <>
              Following the {networks.join(" or ")} link in the footer leaves this site, and
              that visit is handled under {networks.map((n) => `${n}'s`).join(" or ")} own
              terms rather than this policy; this site sends nothing to
              {networks.length > 1 ? " either" : " it"} until you tap.
            </>
          )
        }
      </p>
      <p class="page__body">
        Messages sent to the email addresses on the <a href="/contact">contact</a> page
        are kept only to answer them.
      </p>

      <h2 class="page__sub">Asking for it to be removed</h2>
      <p class="page__body">
        Ask on the <a href="/contact">contact</a> page with your order reference and the
        record will be deleted, except where a payment record has to be kept to account
        for money that actually moved.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page {
    background-color: var(--bg);
    color: var(--fg);
    padding-block: var(--s-56) var(--s-80);
  }

  .page__inner {
    max-width: var(--max-width);
  }

  .page__heading {
    font-size: var(--t-heading);
    margin-block-end: var(--s-40);
  }

  .page__sub {
    font-size: var(--t-label);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-label);
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    margin-block-end: var(--s-16);
    margin-block-start: var(--s-40);
  }

  .page__body {
    color: var(--fg-muted);
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-block-end: var(--s-20);
  }

  .page__hair {
    border: 0;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--border);
    width: 100%;
    margin-block: var(--s-40);
  }
</style>
